{"tool_name":"promod3","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"promod3","version":"3.6.0","home":"https://openstructure.org/promod3/","documentation":"https://openstructure.org/promod3/","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"ProMod3 is a tool for protein structure prediction and refinement","identifiers":["biotools:promod3","doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1008667"],"description":"ProMod3 is a modelling engine based on the OpenStructure computational\nstructural biology framework (www.openstructure.org)\nthat can perform all steps required to generate a protein model by\nhomology. Its modular design aims at implementing flexible modelling\npipelines and fast prototyping of novel algorithms.\n","license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"number":1,"run_exports":[null],"skip":true},"requirements":{"build":[null,null,"cmake","ninja","pkg-config"],"host":["python","libboost-devel >=1.86,<1.87","libboost-python-devel >=1.86,<1.87","openmm >=7","eigen","openstructure >=2.11.0"],"run":["python",null]},"source_url":"https://git.scicore.unibas.ch/schwede/ProMod3/-/archive/3.6.0/promod3-3.6.0.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["pm 2>&1 | grep -q Usage","pip check"],"imports":["promod3"],"requires":["pip"],"source_files":["doc/tests/data/1crn.fasta","doc/tests/data/1crn_cut.pdb","doc/tests/data/1CRNA.hhm"]}},"biotools":{"id":"promod3","home":"https://openstructure.org/promod3/","summary":"ProMod3 is a versatile homology modelling toolbox.\n\nProMod3 is a modelling engine based on the OpenStructure [biasini2013] computational structural biology framework that can perform all steps required to generate a protein model by homology. Its modular design aims at implementing flexible modelling pipelines and fast prototyping of novel algorithms.","addition_date":"2021-03-19T08:51:52Z","last_update_date":"2021-03-30T12:09:47Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:promod3","credit":[{"email":"torsten.schwede@unibas.ch","name":"Torsten Schwede","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2715-335X","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Database search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2421"},{"term":"Protein modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0477"},{"term":"Protein structure validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0321"},{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292"}]}],"name":"ProMod3","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/JOURNAL.PCBI.1008667","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021 Studer et al.Computational methods for protein structure modelling are routinely used to complement experimental structure determination, thus they help to address a broad spectrum of scientific questions in biomedical research. The most accurate methods today are based on homology modelling, i.e. detecting a homologue to the desired target sequence that can be used as a template for modelling. Here we present a versatile open source homology modelling toolbox as foundation for flexible and computationally efficient modelling workflows. Pro- Mod3 is a fully scriptable software platform that can perform all steps required to generate a protein model by homology. Its modular design aims at fast prototyping of novel algorithms and implementing flexible modelling pipelines. Common modelling tasks, such as loop modelling, sidechain modelling or generating a full protein model by homology, are provided as production ready pipelines, forming the starting point for own developments and enhancements. ProMod3 is the central software component of the widely used SWISSMODEL web-server.","authors":[{"name":"Biasini M."},{"name":"Bienert S."},{"name":"Johner N."},{"name":"Schwede T."},{"name":"Studer G."},{"name":"Tauriello G."}],"citationCount":10,"date":"2021-01-28T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title":"ProMod3 - A versatile homology modelling toolbox"},"pmcid":"PMC7872268","pmid":"3